2.
 CGG policy rule estimate
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{eqnarray*}
r_{t}^{*} & = & \beta E_{t}\left\{ \pi_{t+1}\right\} +\gamma\chi_{t}\\
r_{t} & = & \rho r_{t-1}+(1-\rho)r_{t}^{*}
\end{eqnarray*}

\end_inset

where 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho$
\end_inset

 is known as inflation rate inertia, 
\begin_inset Formula $\chi_{t}$
\end_inset

 is the output gap, 
\begin_inset Formula $r_{t}$
\end_inset

 is the nominal interest rate, and 
\begin_inset Formula $r_{t}^{*}$
\end_inset

 is the target rate.
 They estimate the parameters by using the data associated with the previous
 table.
 Important to note, the central bank changes its behaviors by altering the
 following parameter values.
